{"name":"Turf War","hex":"#738050","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"turf war","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dispute over territory between rival gangs.","A fight or confrontation between two divisions or parties for access to resources or capital."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/turf_war"}],"entries":[{"title":"Daggermouth","blocks":[{"text":"Daggermouth was a Canadian pop punk band that formed in 2004 in Vancouver, British Columbia. They started around early 2004 and toured with bands such as Moneen and SNFU. They broke up in 2008 and returned for a reunion in 2018."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daggermouth"},{"title":"Filmtracks 2000","blocks":[{"text":"Filmtracks 2000 is the thirteenth album by American composer Bill Laswell, released on September 25, 2001 by Tzadik Records. Despite the title's suggestion, the album is not a collection of Laswell's film scores. Instead it is an assemblage of new compositions which contain the hallmarks of soundtrack music, drawing influences from the music of India, Asia and the Middle East."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/1/14/Bill_Laswell_-_Filmtracks_2000.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filmtracks_2000"},{"title":"Turf War (The Office)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Turf War\" is the twenty-third and penultimate episode of the eighth season of the American comedy television series The Office, and the show's 175th episode overall. The episode originally aired on NBC on May 3, 2012. \"Turf War\" was written by Warren Lieberstein and Halsted Sullivan, and was directed by Daniel Chun. The episode guest stars Chris Bauer, Andy Buckley, and Dan Castellaneta."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turf_War_(The_Office)"},{"title":"Sod","blocks":[{"text":"Sod is the upper layer of turf that is harvested for transplanting. Turf consists of a variable thickness of a 